# Local Development Secrets Template
# ==================================
#
# Copy this file to .dev.vars and fill in your values:
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# These secrets are used by `wrangler dev` for local development.
# NEVER commit .dev.vars to version control!
#
# For production, set these secrets via wrangler:
#   npx wrangler secret put GITHUB_CLIENT_ID
#   npx wrangler secret put GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET
#   npx wrangler secret put SESSION_SECRET

# GitHub OAuth App Credentials
# Create an OAuth App at: https://github.com/settings/developers
# Set the callback URL to: http://localhost:8787/auth/github/callback (for local dev)
# or https://your-domain.com/auth/github/callback (for production)
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your_github_client_id_here
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=your_github_client_secret_here

# Session Secret
# Used to sign session cookies. Generate a random string:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# or use: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
SESSION_SECRET=your_random_session_secret_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional settings (leave unset unless you need them)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Explicit OAuth callback URL (recommended for production). If unset, the OAuth
# flow falls back to the request origin.
# OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8787/auth/github/callback

# Global edge cache purging after admin actions (custom-domain deployments only).
# Both must be set together: a Cloudflare zone ID and an API token with the
# "Cache Purge" permission scoped to that zone. If unset, purging falls back to
# the local PoP only. See docs/CACHING.md.
# CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=your_zone_id_here
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your_cache_purge_token_here
